{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded","id":168314,"title":"Power of Dragon Blooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-13T15:50:53-07:00","id":168314,"title":"Power of Dragon Blooded","content":"Ciao.<br /> First of all:<br /> I'm only begin to read Exalted, I played no games, and generaly - I'm noob. So my question can be stupid.<br /> I really can't image the power level of average or elder Dragon-blooded. I mean, I have no reference point or an example for comparison. Charms' discription (2ed edition) seems like ability of normal bad-ass/peak of human, and some of the most magical powers seems... well, like powers of average mutant of Marvel-verse.<br /> Is it right level of dragon-blooded?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T16:14:52-07:00","id":168348,"title":"","content":"Barring one single charm in their whole charmset, pretty much. Marvel mutants vary quite a bit, but they're not a bad place to look. The Human Torch might be a good example of an elder fire aspect, similarly the thing an elder earth aspect. Younger DBs are probably more along the lines of Gambit or there abouts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T16:28:00-07:00","id":168352,"title":"","content":"Actually Avatar the Last Airbender and Legend of Korra are good places to look. TenIn and Bei Fong are basically the mayor and sherif of bosstown and definitely great examples of master air and earth aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T02:12:09-07:00","id":168736,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> Andwhat is this single charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T04:02:25-07:00","id":168770,"title":"","content":"It's a tad bit more complex than that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T04:48:01-07:00","id":168790,"title":"","content":"What do you mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T05:01:38-07:00","id":168797,"title":"","content":"Well, there are two ways to look at power.<br /> <br /> One is what the power of an (elder) Dragon-Blooded is supposed to be according to the setting of the edition (presumably Second Edition). This way is more or less static throughout an edition.<br /> <br /> The other is to look at Charms and other mechanical manifestations of Dragon-Blooded power, to look at the system, to gauge what the power of Dragon-Blooded is. However, this power level is in flux. It started somewhere in the 2E Corebook, it varied with the splatbooks and the errata's of the 2E, and finally it changed once again with the 2.5 fix.<br /> <br /> So, you'll have to be more precise in your question to get a more precise answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T05:10:56-07:00","id":168799,"title":"","content":"I guess one static point of reference you can use is that, sans equipment bonuses, the absolute most dice an ordinary mortal can apply to an action is 13. If you exceed this number you are in superhuman territory. With excellencies alone, a dragonblood can hit peak mortal at what they would consider average competency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T05:19:17-07:00","id":168801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=168799#post168799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess one static point of reference you can use is that, sans equipment bonuses, the absolute most dice an ordinary mortal can apply to an action is 13. If you exceed this number you are in superhuman territory. With excellencies alone, a dragonblood can hit peak mortal at what they would consider average competency.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The absolute number of dice a heroic mortal can apply <b>prior to any magic accessible to mortals</b> is well over 20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T05:25:32-07:00","id":168806,"title":"","content":"I was ignoring stunts and virtue channelling because they're kinda situational and also exalts can do that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T05:57:13-07:00","id":168822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emeraldstreak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=168797#post168797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there are two ways to look at power.<br /> <br /> One is what the power of an (elder) Dragon-Blooded is supposed to be according to the setting of the edition (presumably Second Edition). This way is more or less static throughout an edition.<br /> <br /> The other is to look at Charms and other mechanical manifestations of Dragon-Blooded power, to look at the system, to gauge what the power of Dragon-Blooded is. However, this power level is in flux. It started somewhere in the 2E Corebook, it varied with the splatbooks and the errata's of the 2E, and finally it changed once again with the 2.5 fix.<br /> <br /> So, you'll have to be more precise in your question to get a more precise answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. For example - if we compare the average dragon blooded fighter (Air) of 2.5 edition with some super-hero, who will be this superhero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T08:16:37-07:00","id":168942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=168822#post168822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> OK. For example - if we compare the average dragon blooded fighter (Air) of 2.5 edition with some super-hero, who will be this superhero?</div> </div> </div> </div> The competency level of the average marvel superhero.....dragon bloods are about on par with captain america. the x-men are a good analogy. With a few exceptions, the x-men are on the lower scale of power in marvel. they are competent fighters, but its their (often elemental in nature) powers that push them into the superhuman territory. the same can be said of dragon bloods. their level of compentency doesnt rise much higher than that of a heroic mortal, but the fact that they can shoot blasts of fire, toughen their skin like rock and control the winds makes them more powerful via capability, not necesarily competency. Celestial exalted are at the power level of say the fantastic four or the avengers. they are in general nearly an order of magnitude more powerful than the x-men. they command greater powers with a greater level of competency. Solars, abyssals and infernals are on the level of cosmic beings. heralds of galactus and the like. an order of magnitude more powerful than the avengers. In general, it would take several x-men to take down a single avenger and several avengers to take down a single herald of galactus. There are characters who break these rules of course. as x-men characters, prof X and magneto are both very powerful....as least equal to an avenger. storm is also on that level when she pushes herself. and wolverines fighting competency is nigh equal to captain americas and well, he can't die under normal circumstances. dark phoenix is on the level of a herald of galactus at least (possibly more) but she's a special case. Then you have the characters on the next power level above a herald of galactus. Thanos, apocalypse, galactus, the eternals etc. these would be the deathlords, 3rd circle demons, celestial deities etc. beings more powerful than even the solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T08:54:21-07:00","id":168965,"title":"","content":"Intresting. When you said &quot;Celestial&quot;, you means Lunars and Sederial? So, one more question^ I also ask, how powerful average Alchemical-elder and average Lunar-elder can be (in terms of Marvel verse)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T09:28:14-07:00","id":168986,"title":"","content":"A celestial exalt is any that has an Incarna for a patron. Which is pretty much everything but dragon blooded. Even Alchies count for certain effects. <br /> <br /> As far as Elder Alchemical power goes, picture Optimus Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T10:26:10-07:00","id":169019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=168965#post168965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intresting. When you said &amp;quot;Celestial&amp;quot;, you means Lunars and Sederial? So, one more question^ I also ask, how powerful average Alchemical-elder and average Lunar-elder can be (in terms of Marvel verse)?</div> </div> </div> </div> Among the exalted, there are three &quot;tiers&quot; of power. terrestrial (dragon bloods) celestial (lunars, sidereals, alchemicals etc) and solar (solars, abyssals and infernals). Although the term celestial exalted refers to all the exalted above terrestrial level as mentioned above, solars (and their corrupted versions) are a step up in power from the other celestial exalted, thus they occupy a tier of power all their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T11:14:58-07:00","id":169037,"title":"","content":"So, average Lunar-elder can be analogy of top marvel-Heroes (like Thor)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T11:36:02-07:00","id":169047,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I dunno. Thor is usually put on a tier with the Hulk, and the Hulk could conceivably give Isidoros a run for his money in the brute force arena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T12:07:19-07:00","id":169078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169047#post169047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I dunno. Thor is usually put on a tier with the Hulk, and the Hulk could conceivably give Isidoros a run for his money in the brute force arena.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this may be why the devs have said that thinking in tiers would be an unhelpful prospect in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T12:09:19-07:00","id":169101,"title":"","content":"It's really best not to overthink comic book power levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T12:42:53-07:00","id":169125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169101#post169101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really best not to overthink comic book power levels.</div> </div> </div> </div> Indeed. comic book writers are notoriously inconsistent on how they present the power level of their characters. however if one is fairly familiar with the characters in question, its pretty easy to extrapolate an average level of power for the characters as to where they fall in relation to other characters in the universe. i tend to find marvel to be more consistent than DC but ultimately that's not saying much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T12:44:12-07:00","id":169126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169101#post169101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really best not to overthink comic book power levels.</div> </div> </div> </div> I just use comic characters as example. Now, average Dragon-blooded sems (for me) as Gambit with skills and trainig of Nigthwing. And, may be, with magic (but I don't know, how Terrestial magic strong). Anyway, not bad (considering, that they are the weakest Exalted).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T12:47:25-07:00","id":169141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169037#post169037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, average Lunar-elder can be analogy of top marvel-Heroes (like Thor)?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, thats a pretty good guideline. your average solar is going to fall around that power level as well and elder solars will hit the next power tier (silver surfer, firelord, gladiator etc.) I would say that Thanos with the infinity gauntlet would be at the power of the primordials at the height of their power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T13:16:48-07:00","id":169174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=168822#post168822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK. For example - if we compare the average dragon blooded fighter (Air) of 2.5 edition with some super-hero, who will be this superhero?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In 2.5, a Dragon-Blooded compares well to a superhero...for a short while only. Exalted in 2.5 spend too many net motes at top power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T15:25:05-07:00","id":169300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=168736#post168736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks.<br /> <br /> Andwhat is this single charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably <i>As in the Beginning</i> (which is basically a nuke, causing a massive elemental conflagration that totally annihilated anything in a multiple-miles radius), although <i>Wrath-Directing Gesture</i> also qualifies IMHO. Both are War charms. DB War had this problem in 2e where it had charms that made war itself irrelevant because one elder could do more damage than the Realm's entire armies. I recall back when we would discuss hypothetical war scenarios, the most pressing question wouldn't be about the Realm's military or its vast empire, but how many E7 Exalts it had capable of using <i>As In the Beginning</i> and how rapidly it could move them around.<br /> <br /> That... will probably not be something DBs do in 3e. And those charms stuck out as out-of-place among the rest of the DB charmset, which was generally much more down to earth, or which focused on more low-level superheroic elemental powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 06-14-2014, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T15:46:27-07:00","id":169305,"title":"","content":"Eh, it's channelling the elements themselves in a big, dramatic fashion. Seems in-theme, even if it is a bit OP. It's got nothing on what a solar of that level could do though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T16:01:10-07:00","id":169312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169305#post169305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, it's channelling the elements themselves in a big, dramatic fashion. Seems in-theme, even if it is a bit OP. It's got nothing on what a solar of that level could do though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it is exactly equivalent in radius to the closest-comparable E7 Solar Melee charm, and significantly more damaging; it also significantly outdamages <i>Rain of Doom</i>, the trademark city-smashing Sorcery spell, while being cheaper and much much easier to use.<br /> <br /> However, that's not really the important part; the big problem is that if DBs have War charms like that, then their entire structure and place in the story (as magically-empowered families who build a great empire and use its might to extend their reach) falls apart. The Realm itself ceases to matter, because a single determined elder with that charm and some fast transportation can do more damage, alone, than all of his descendents and all of their armies and wealth combined.<br /> <br /> That is <i>occasionally</i> acceptable for Solars, Infernals, and Abyssals, because they're supposed to have this theme of cataclysmic potential, that you can't allow even one of them to survive or they will present a dramatic threat to Creation at some point in the future; but DBs don't work that way. One DB elder is very dangerous in many ways, but that doesn't extend to &quot;can dissolve cities with a single charm activation and a wave of their hand.&quot; I'm not just talking about power here, but theme -- although the two are entwined, of course, especially when it comes to DBs, it's important to underline how DB elders work. They're cunning patriarchs and matriarchs, or ancient, highly-skilled veteran soldiers, or mysterious and dangerous sorcerers; but they're not people who personally walk around blowing up cities, and if you give them that kind of power then a lot of their other themes become irrelevant.<br /> <br /> A DB elder has vast power and talent, but if they want large-scale achievements, they generally have to play the political game to do it -- that's the whole reason the Realm is what it is. If a DB elder wants to destroy a city, they'll send an army.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T16:26:27-07:00","id":169322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=168352#post168352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually Avatar the Last Airbender and Legend of Korra are good places to look...</div> </div> </div> </div>For a bunch of <a href=\"http://youtu.be/j3dT8oK7y80\" target=\"_blank\">awesome, elemental powers</a> that Dragon Blooded will never have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T16:29:11-07:00","id":169324,"title":"","content":"It does require breeding 5, which IIRC is supposed to be fairly rare in the current setting, so the number of DBs with it is probably fairly low. <br /> <br /> Also with the right combination of charms and equipment a solar can go a hell of a long way in an hour so rain of doom potentially has an enormous area of effect. Besides, I've never thought it made sense for Solar Circle Sorcery to have anything resembling an upper limit on what it could do. It's what the primordials used to <i>invent</i> upper limits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T19:03:29-07:00","id":169401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169322#post169322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a bunch of <a href=\"http://youtu.be/j3dT8oK7y80\" target=\"_blank\">awesome, elemental powers</a> that Dragon Blooded will never have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno.<br /> The main reason that power level can't work in 2nd edition is that once you acquire the charm that lets you lay waste to an entire kingdom there's no reason not to use it against say... bandits, because disproportionate retribution is hilarious hence why stuff like As In the Beginning is tucked away at essence 7 out of the hands of player characters. There's no sense of climactic battle or once a century power boosts, the best we have is &quot;you can do the awesome thing and they you fall down dead&quot; via Martyr effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T19:10:46-07:00","id":169408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169324#post169324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does require breeding 5, which IIRC is supposed to be fairly rare in the current setting, so the number of DBs with it is probably fairly low.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that was something that often came up in discussions of the Realm's military power, too. How powerful the Realm was in 2e was heavily dependent on how many elder DBs it had with breeding 5 and, therefore, how many DBs it had capable of using <i>As In the Beginning</i>. This was vastly more significant than, say, the Realm itself, or the legions, or the wealth and power that the Realm was made to hold. Think about that for a moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's what the primordials used to <i>invent</i> upper limits. </div> </div> </div>Explicitly linking Sorcery to the Primordials in 2e was such a terrible terrible idea.<br /> <br /> I have faith that it is not a mistake that 3e will repeat, because it's going to be trying to avoid turning Creation into The Primordial Show again. But I felt compelled to point it out because you're fixing on 2e's link between the Primordials and Sorcery as the cool defining thing about Sorcery that makes it what it is. Solar Circle Sorcery is what it is because of the power of the narratives of magic and sorcery that it draws on, and because of the narratives of sorcerers and magic that are central to people like the Twilight caste, not because of an easter-egg linking it some dumb imprisoned supergods that 2e made the mistake of giving way more attention than it deserved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 06-15-2014, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T20:41:59-07:00","id":169438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169324#post169324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does require breeding 5, which IIRC is supposed to be fairly rare in the current setting, so the number of DBs with it is probably fairly low.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. One of the 100s of things that are supposed to be rare, yet are cheaply obtainable at chargen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T00:56:22-07:00","id":169582,"title":"","content":"Indeed. I think probably about 20% of PCs have Breeding 5... it ought to be more like 1%. And most of those who don't have Breeding 5 have Breeding 3 (because you can get it out of your 12 background points easily, without spending the 4 freebies for Breeding 5).<br /> If people don't have Breeding 3, it's probably because they're deliberately playing a lost egg or outcaste (though some of them have Breeding 3 anyway... which can lead to interesting backstories!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, that was something that often came up in discussions of the Realm's military power, too. How powerful the Realm was in 2e was heavily dependent on how many elder DBs it had with breeding 5 and, therefore, how many DBs it had capable of using <i>As In the Beginning</i>. This was vastly more significant than, say, the Realm itself, or the legions, or the wealth and power that the Realm was made to hold. Think about that for a moment. </div> </div> </div>Even the Essence 5 battle blasting power was a problem. It detracted from the characters themselves (as did As In The Beginning). For example, in the long-running DB game I played, two of the characters were brilliant genius generals, that was their character concept. And of course they had high Intelligence, Command, and War 5, and lots of War charms.<br /> And when they fought battles... was it their brilliant strategy that mattered. No. All of their many War charms were made obselete by that final charm for nuking whole battlefields. No strategy, no genuis, no using the charm for making earthworks, or the charm for making their troops tougher, or having less fatigue. Just a giant fire or lightning bomb.<br /> As In the Beginning is even worse, because it doesn't matter at all that the person using it has War 7 and is one of the greatest generals in Creation, probably one of the greatest in the Realm, they're just a walking nuke cannon.<br /> <br /> Though, on the other hand, I am somewhat amused by the image that when the Realm is in danger, the Realm's top generals troop over to an island south of the Realm, to its most expensive nursing home, and try and convince an extremely senile and confused Ragara to help them, except he keeps telling them to go away because he doesn't want to buy anything today. Or thinks they're Mnemon and tries to kill them. Eventually they convince him, and wheel him to the battlefield, only to find he's forgotten why he's there again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-15-2014, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T01:50:40-07:00","id":169622,"title":"","content":"Well of course 20% of PCs have breeding 5. They're the PCs. In a given game, what percentage of dragonblooded are PCs? Much, much less than 1%","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T02:03:06-07:00","id":169628,"title":"","content":"Ha, I see your point.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But still, I don't like the way everyone takes high breeding because it's cheap, and really good. When someone comes along and goes &quot;I want to play a lost egg, that'd be a cool role-playing experience&quot; they're also down 14 motes. And for a starting DB, that might be like half their essence pool. They're already taking non-mechanical social penalties (and maybe actual penalties from having a worse character creation system, depending on the ST), the essence loss just seems cruel. I don't like overly punishing people for playing interesting characters.<br /> Essentially, breeding is under-priced (especially for high-xp games).<br /> So, I'd be very happy if a high breeding merit worked like Holden has suggested, giving social benefits and a higher chance of having DB kids, because then it'd be something people would take because they're going &quot;I think it'd be cool to play a guy from House V'neef who has excellent breeding, everyone treats him well, but maybe this means they'll be even more anal about who he marries, that'll be a fun character&quot; as opposed to &quot;my concept is Dragonblood master swordsman, I could spend my freebies on better physical stats or more melee charms or maybe an awesome magic sword or mentor who can teach me Even Blade style... nah, I'll take Breeding 5 for the motes&quot;. Essentially, buying something which is very fluff-important, for entirely unrelated reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T02:12:59-07:00","id":169633,"title":"","content":"I feel that having access to a nuke charm does very much turn large scale tactical considerations into nuke dropping contests, very much as it did so in real life (when you have access to nuclear weapons, and so does your enemy, your biggest concern is thermonuclear warfare), and that this takes away from the Dragonblooded more than it does anyone else (as their whole military empire shebang with legions etc is kind of undermined with nukes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T02:35:05-07:00","id":169639,"title":"","content":"You can't assassinate a nuke though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T04:21:08-07:00","id":169693,"title":"","content":"Assassination only works when the Dragon-Blooded in question is nowhere near the intended target, otherwise killing them only reduces the time anyone in the target area has to get away.<br /> I've had this cool mental image of a group of PCs saving a city by persuading a Dragon-Blooded elder to show mercy, sadly with social combat that's very problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T05:05:47-07:00","id":169702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emeraldstreak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the 100s of things that are supposed to be rare, yet are cheaply obtainable at chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Mathamatics are biased in favour of players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T05:10:00-07:00","id":169704,"title":"","content":"AitB sounds a bit like it mess up the Realm Civil War quite a bit.<br /> <br /> This is one of those things where I wish the game was clearer on treating the power / pure energy and finesse / integration of a character's Essence separately. If it was clear that Dragonblooded elders had a lot more finesse and integration of their Essence and only a little bit more power / energy, that would get us to a more intutive reason why a mega &quot;Dragon Vortex attack&quot; wouldn't make a lot of sense, and generally what their high level magic would look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T05:13:32-07:00","id":169706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never thought it made sense for Solar Circle Sorcery to have anything resembling an upper limit on what it could do. It's what the primordials used to invent upper limits.</div> </div> </div> </div> An impressive statement, and an incoherent mechanic; perfect defenses writ large.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T05:28:42-07:00","id":169710,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that Tepet Arada, called &quot;The most decorated Dynastic military leader alive&quot; in Scroll of Exalts, only has war 5. Given that outside the realm breeding 5 is almost unheard of it seems reasonable to conclude that AitB is a lost art, and nobody in Creation actually knows it unless it serves your game to say otherwise. At most there's probably a dozen individuals who qualify and since they are all elders of impeccable pedigree in their late 200s they probably have better shit to do than run from battle to battle nuking things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T05:35:22-07:00","id":169711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169633#post169633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that having access to a nuke charm does very much turn large scale tactical considerations into nuke dropping contests, very much as it did so in real life (when you have access to nuclear weapons, and so does your enemy, your biggest concern is thermonuclear warfare), and that this takes away from the Dragonblooded more than it does anyone else (as their whole military empire shebang with legions etc is kind of undermined with nukes).</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree. To be fair, with the civil war, the more common Essence 5 nuke charm isn't so much a problem, because the first charm in the War tree allows a DB leader to protect his troops from it. But AitB would, as Ghosthead says, still screw things up.<br /> Tepet Ejava? Who cares, she doesn't have AitB. Mnemon maybe might have it, in which case she'll probably win (though one could argue it'd be seen as a colossal war crime). Although probably 4 or 5 others (who'd probably need the agathic drugs, but those are common for important DBs) would have it too. So it'd be less a civil war and more just an assassination match, and then one side wins. Like the Cold War, a lot of which was about getting the upper hand in nuke deployment or acquiring related technology (like stealth bombers).<br /> Which is interesting in some ways, but probably not the most genre-appropriate way to sort it out.<br /> You could, of course, just have everyone assassinate each others' elders who have the charm early on, but it seems weird to have the whole civil war hinge on this charm.<br /> Probably the easiest thing is just to say it's a lost charm in the 2nd age, not enough people get to War 7 that anyone's redeveloped it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, even the regular nuke charms (the essence 5 ones) severely distort the Realm's wars in the Threshold, as I agree that it detracts from their Imperial conquest style, with all those big armies. The general using charms to make his troops really awesome, that's fine, but just blowing the enemy to smithereens makes all those soldiers fairly pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T05:38:56-07:00","id":169714,"title":"","content":"Not Roseblack, Her grandad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T06:03:31-07:00","id":169736,"title":"","content":"It's one of the few charms that we know for a fact the Scarlet Empress has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T06:27:59-07:00","id":169743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169702#post169702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Mathamatics are biased in favour of players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in DnD 4E maybe.<br /> <br /> In Exalted, NPCs use the same chargen rules + tons of extra XP if Elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T07:09:30-07:00","id":169762,"title":"","content":"Eh, honestly it's not that much XP. No way is a PC who's been playing for 10 years of game time going to only have 100xp. More like 1000. Or more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T07:14:27-07:00","id":169764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169582#post169582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the Essence 5 battle blasting power was a problem. It detracted from the characters themselves (as did As In The Beginning). For example, in the long-running DB game I played, two of the characters were brilliant genius generals, that was their character concept. And of course they had high Intelligence, Command, and War 5, and lots of War charms.<br /> And when they fought battles... was it their brilliant strategy that mattered. No. All of their many War charms were made obselete by that final charm for nuking whole battlefields. No strategy, no genuis, no using the charm for making earthworks, or the charm for making their troops tougher, or having less fatigue. Just a giant fire or lightning bomb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I think the problem there was less that it was a nuke as such, and more that it's an area denial weapon that the players insisted on using as if it were a nuke (and then complaining when it didn't in fact behave like a nuke). That does suggest that it's probably overpowered for what it's supposed to be doing, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":978,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","user":"Iozz-Sothoth","date":". 06-15-2014, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T07:28:38-07:00","id":169772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emeraldstreak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169743#post169743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Exalted, NPCs use the same chargen rules + tons of extra XP if Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except NPCs don't get to <i>choose</i> whether they have high Breeding or not, because that would be nonsensical. How easy it is to get in chargen is only important for players, because you're just going to give to your NPCs whatever makes sense for them to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T08:19:05-07:00","id":169787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169772#post169772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except NPCs don't get to <i>choose</i> whether they have high Breeding or not, because that would be nonsensical. How easy it is to get in chargen is only important for players, because you're just going to give to your NPCs whatever makes sense for them to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>The important thing people forget. Whether mortal, Dragon-Blooded, or Solar, Exalted is not D&amp;D; you do not start as a level 1 dirt farmer unless you choose to start as a dirt farmer. The players are meant to start as important figures and grow exponentially so, not be &quot;just another of the little fish in the big pond&quot;.<br /> <br /> The objective of Exalted shouldn't be &quot;Encourage Dragon-BLooded PCs to start with Breeding 0-1 because you're impotent weakling byblows of the dragons, not IMPORTANT ones&quot;, but should be &quot;Make Breeding competitive with other backgrounds/merits/etc, rather than overpoweringly good, so that people who want to be a lost egg don't feel supremely weakened by not being Breeding 3-5, while those who want to be of the purest dragon blood can take Breeding 5 and feel justified in that decision&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's a tough call, but the objective of &quot;Don't tell PCs they're not important enough to have X in their story&quot; is one of the big things that keeps me coming back to Exalted despite 2e's poor handling of Sidereals and Lunars, anti-Infernal rage, Solar importance overinflation...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 06-15-2014, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T10:06:23-07:00","id":169875,"title":"","content":"Most of the time my stance is &quot;make the character you want to make, because the game ls not meant to be optimized and doing so will worsen your experience&quot;, but I can't really get down on people for bull-rushing (traditional) Breeding, because it's just so incredibly excessive a benefit, and because the benefit it provides is critical to absolutely every DB character -- not just &quot;critical if other people are optimizing and the ST isn't calibrating difficulty to the party&quot;, but <i>actually critical</i> since DBs have tiny mote pools and are not very well put together in 2e. It's incredibly onerous in a way that a lot of other things people complain about aren't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T10:13:10-07:00","id":169876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emeraldstreak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Exalted, NPCs use the same chargen rules + tons of extra XP if Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div> No longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T10:34:32-07:00","id":169911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169633#post169633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that having access to a nuke charm does very much turn large scale tactical considerations into nuke dropping contests, very much as it did so in real life (when you have access to nuclear weapons, and so does your enemy, your biggest concern is thermonuclear warfare)</div> </div> </div> </div>Disregarding the Age of Sorrows, I feel as though the overall setting is more amenable to a varied tactical and strategic profile when it comes to weapons operating on a scale comparable to nuclear arms since there's likely to be a more varied and effective range of defensive options for dealing with them, up to and including going forth to do battle against them.<br /> <br /> I'd also feel that the setting would provide more options for the aftermath of such strikes (and not in the form of shadowlands) that make for interesting local alterations in their own right. Like, if a faerie host sends forth a dragon with the Wyld bellowing in their stomach to be turned to fire on their breath, maybe they burn a few cities before it's put down, but now you have a new Wyld zone, probably with its own unique prodigies within to harvest.<br /> <br /> These things are uncommon in the Age of Sorrows, mind, and shouldn't really form a mainstay of strategic doctrines. More half understood weapons of last resort (which is the impression given by the first write up of Lookshy's arsenal, including the thing that became the soulbreaker orb). Between such things and various monsters, Creation is likely scarred and pockmarked with all manner of unusual twisted landscapes, waiting to be investigated and tamed (or fenced off for the good of all).<br /> <br /> But yes, I don't really like the idea of any Exalt being equivalent to a tactical nuke through the use of their own Charms. Artifacts (whether storied weapons or elaborate designs), sorcery, chained or allied beasts, things like that, things that the Exalted can bend to their will through their prowess, which itself plays out at a more personal level. Let the dragon be the one who levels cities in a single action, while you're the honeyed voice moving his heart.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T11:43:18-07:00","id":169958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=169762#post169762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, honestly it's not that much XP. No way is a PC who's been playing for 10 years of game time going to only have 100xp. More like 1000. Or more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it depends on how that time was passed. If everyone's character has settled down into a stable routine, 10 years can pass as quickly as the ST saying &quot;Ten years later...&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T12:01:59-07:00","id":169966,"title":"","content":"The only thing that an Essence 7 charm really matters for is the picture it paints of high-essence characters, and the way that picture causes players to think about characters more generally. As In the Beginning fails this test pretty hard -- really, the Scroll of Errata charms are the only high-essence charms in the line that didn't totally fuck up on that count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T13:21:14-07:00","id":170065,"title":"","content":"OK, what about non-fight charms? Comparing with mortal doctor how good Wood Dragon-Blooded as hiller if his medicine charms is developed for maximum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T14:54:47-07:00","id":170138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=170065#post170065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, what about non-fight charms? Comparing with mortal doctor how good Wood Dragon-Blooded as hiller if his medicine charms is developed for maximum?</div> </div> </div> </div>This...is a somewhat complicated and controversial answer. If you look through all the DB charm trees you'll notice that their presence tree has charms that grant health levels and shout at people until they explode, performance has charms to do street brawls in secret and kill people with your music and medicine has at least one charm for infecting people with horrible disease.<br /> <br /> Basically even when DBs are investing in areas that aren't fighty...they're still being fighty about it. Hell even lore has, I think, one charm to actually assist in lore and then six charms based on killing people with fire and regenerate health and stuff. Medicine is one of the few places where they only have one or two charms that help directly in combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, some people like this because it makes DBs unique an interesting. You don't always have to be afraid of the combat skills of even a Solar diplomat, I mean you probably should be because he's a Solar and who knows what crazy boulder-punching he does on the side, but it's not for sure. If you're talking to a DB diplomat, almost certainly he has a Terrifying Fire Dragon Roar up his sleeve, and they'd do it after activating Aura of Invulnerability and Glowing Coal Radiance. Compared to a mortal that makes him a fairly formidable opponent, and he's just a really damn good talker.<br /> <br /> The downside is that if you want to play a fantastic orator or musician there's really only one charm in the performance set that helps you do that. It's a pretty good one, but it's also pretty focused. You can't do something like raise the ground up to make a podium or forum or stage or whatever that gives you bonuses or anything like that, your magic just lets you incite riots. On the other hand you can melt people's faces off with a guitar solo or maim somebody in the street and people will just assume it's an act. You could even melt somebody's face in the street and people around you will assume it's just some street play. So you're an excellent assassin but not a particularly powerful performer.<br /> <br /> <br /> For medicine in particular, DBs have pretty much a full suite of charms to deal with poison, infection and wounds. They can turn any lethal wound into a bad bruise with a single touch, for instance. Their magic usually fails against other magic until they're very old though. Magical diseases require essence 4 and it takes an immense effort to cure aggravated damage. So you'll never get your bruises mended but they can turn you from a bloody mess into somebody who's just black and blue, it's pretty hard on them though. Also they can not re-attach anything that's fallen off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T15:06:51-07:00","id":170149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=170138#post170138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell even lore has, I think, one charm to actually assist in lore...</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, they have TWO of those. :P<br /> <br /> One to speed up learning, and another for perfect remembrance. (It's weaker and a lot costlier than the Lunar one, though.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T15:36:17-07:00","id":170161,"title":"","content":"Bureaucracy is also devoid of charms that will aid in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T15:52:12-07:00","id":170168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=170161#post170161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bureaucracy is also devoid of charms that will aid in a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div> Right yes, the one charmset that has no combat charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T16:02:47-07:00","id":170173,"title":"","content":"I'm looking at the 1e book here (2e might be a little different) but Dragonblooded cascades do vary. What gets published for them, for Dynasts, typically is all about being kind of generally warrior-cum-aristocratic. (We can kind of assume this is written into their nature or we're just seeing Charms which reflect Dynastic culture, to taste.)<br /> <br /> A Dragonblooded diplomat who relies on Presence, would be formidable in battle (that cascade is war oriented), where one who relies on Linguistics or Bureaucracy, really wouldn't.<br /> <br /> With performance in particular, aristocrats aren't really the &quot;I perform to impress you&quot; sort of people, so it looks like inspiration was not forthcoming there, so thus, &quot;my magic is fight&quot;. By contrast they have fair amounts of suitably aristo stuff in socialise. They have a fair amount for anything intrigue related, because that's their default genre, and are also fairly good at exploring and journeying, doing the sort of trade and organisation running that an aristo would need to, etc.<br /> <br /> (Dragonbloods are also the physically oriented, working caste of the Exalted, so I think they also have some stuff in that direction, that's all about no nonsense using the elements to build and maintain sturdy, durable, functional stuff.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T16:10:52-07:00","id":170179,"title":"","content":"It's difficult to say what aspects of Dragon-Blooded are the fault of their charmset being really old.<br /> The original Solar Lore tree was worse for having little to do with the ability it was based on (the teaching charms weren't introduced until the Caste Books).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T16:13:01-07:00","id":170180,"title":"","content":"You sort of have to avoid stepping on the Solar's toes whilst acknowledging that there should have been some charm development in the areas terrestrials were historically unlikely to occupy in the 1500 years since they nicked their jobs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T13:17:39-07:00","id":170989,"title":"","content":"And now I must ask about Lunars, couse I like this Exalted. How strong they are? Couse some frend told me, that Full Moon Lunar is strong enough to be equal to Abyssal (only in fight, of course). But I more intresting of their power level at all, in &quot;terms of superheroes&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T13:36:33-07:00","id":170999,"title":"","content":"Lunars are <i>supposed </i>to be slightly less powerful than solars but make up for it by being more versatile. How well the mechanics actually achieve this is a matter of intense debate. <br /> <br /> On the whole, a combat-focused lunar beating a solaroid in a one-on-one fight is not an inconceivable outcome. Turning into a Kaiju is one of their simpler tricks at high levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T14:08:42-07:00","id":171018,"title":"","content":"Actual power levels ingame vary a great deal depending on how combat focused and optimized a character is. It's better to imagine power level as a very broad range instead of a fixed point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T14:14:39-07:00","id":171020,"title":"","content":"Thanks, but as I told, I more want to understand their power... you know, as is. May be, comparing with superheroes again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T14:18:01-07:00","id":171024,"title":"","content":"Ok, picture a combination of Animal Man and Beast Boy with magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T14:38:08-07:00","id":171050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 