quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=171081#post171081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not the big comic-fan too (Elfive, I don't even know who is Animal Man <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) But Exalted arequite similar to super-heroes (as I know, there is even altentative modern setting, which is describe in one of books).<br /> <br /> But OK... Can combat-focused Lunar-Elder to make destructions like... like in New York in any sammer blockbaster?</div> </div> </div> </div>That...greatly depends on age and possibly on edition. An elder Lunar in second edition could level New York, like worse than Superman destroyed Metropolis. However I've heard that in third edition they're toning that back a bit so that while you can still do that it might take more effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T15:55:20-07:00","id":171147,"title":"","content":"A lunar optimized for combat can easily equal a Solar/Abyssal in that realm. It is more difficult for Lunars to match Solar class characters in other aspects though. It's the bonuses they achieve from DBT that bring Lunars into parity with Solars combat wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:10:12-07:00","id":174767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=171081#post171081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But OK... Can combat-focused Lunar-Elder to make destructions like... like in New York in any sammer blockbaster?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a matter of whether they can, but - to paraphrase Angua von Ueberwald from the Diskworld - how long do they have to do it. Barring someone strong enough to stop them, a Lunar elder can wreck a mundane place pretty thoroughly either with their personal might, an army, causing widespread riots or via judicious uses of sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T19:09:34-07:00","id":174824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=171020#post171020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, but as I told, I more want to understand their power... you know, as is. May be, comparing with superheroes again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Hulk would be a pretty good idea of what powerlevel, it would look more like the abomination but follow the same ideas, in fact the whole gamma group I think make pretty good examples of ability exalts in general","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T04:36:38-07:00","id":193385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=170989#post170989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now I must ask about Lunars, couse I like this Exalted. How strong they are? Couse some frend told me, that Full Moon Lunar is strong enough to be equal to Abyssal (only in fight, of course). But I more intresting of their power level at all, in &quot;terms of superheroes&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's how celestials stack up in combat:<br /> Solars &gt; Lunars &gt; Abyssals = Infernals (holes in the charmset with 2.5 drag them down) &gt; Sidereals &gt; Dragonblooded<br /> In terms of non-combat things Infernals get ahead of the Lunars, because of the holes in Lunar charmset.<br /> At high essence Infernals get ahead in Mass Combat, by virtue of their Shintais being a horrible holocaust form. Scarlet Rupture Shintai for deals 1L level per tick to everything that doesn't have awakened essence (and drains essence form the others) within 250m radius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T04:54:12-07:00","id":193394,"title":"","content":"What's your reasoning for putting Lunars ahead of Abyssals in combat? I disagree mostly because of Lunars' higher charm costs and higher Charm prereqs for basically everything comparable to Solaroids. The cheap, lazy way to get &quot;balance.&quot; Really Abyssals are Solaroids, it's hard to put anything in front of them, especially Silver Solars. GSPs are just a dip below because of how 2.5 affected their core mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-10-2014, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T05:22:49-07:00","id":193405,"title":"","content":"High essence infernals are an utter wild card because they get to design their own charm set from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T05:27:38-07:00","id":193408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=193405#post193405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High essence infernals are an utter wild card because they get to design their own charm set from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an implied Chicanery-No there, though. I think you have to assume, all things being equal, that a given Devil-Tiger Charmset will be around the same relative power level as existing Yozi Charmsets, just holding different themes and effects (not that your average player or even ST is up to crafting a balanced charmset from scratch).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T06:22:43-07:00","id":193477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=193408#post193408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an implied Chicanery-No there, though. I think you have to assume, all things being equal, that a given Devil-Tiger Charmset will be around the same relative power level as existing Yozi Charmsets, just holding different themes and effects (not that your average player or even ST is up to crafting a balanced charmset from scratch).</div> </div> </div> </div>Being Solaroids, Infernals are supposed to be on the same level as the Solars and Abyssals. And they mostly are. Their problem is the charmset holes, left by transition to 2.5. With the recently published band-aid Malfeans Scourges and Adorjani Slayers get close to solars in murderpower.<br /> Invincible Sword Princess DT has no reasons not to be as good in as Solars in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T06:28:13-07:00","id":193494,"title":"","content":"I still don't get why you ranked Lunars above Abyssals:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=193394#post193394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree mostly because of Lunars' higher charm costs and higher Charm prereqs for basically everything comparable to Solaroids. The cheap, lazy way to get &quot;balance.&quot; Really Abyssals are Solaroids, it's hard to put anything in front of them, especially Silver Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T07:52:19-07:00","id":193584,"title":"","content":"Really, anything as close to &quot;solars but murderyer&quot; as abyssals should be at least as good in a fight. If they somehow manage to not be something has gone horribly wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T09:50:58-07:00","id":193732,"title":"","content":"Essence 5 Abyssals can get Symphony of the Flayed Legion. Boosted by mote feeding charms, it's an 18 miles-radius moving tempest of death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T14:39:24-07:00","id":193987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=193494#post193494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't get why you ranked Lunars above Abyssals:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Spectral and -2 penalty in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T14:47:28-07:00","id":193991,"title":"","content":"Is that the -2 that goes away if you basically dress goth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T16:07:46-07:00","id":194060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=193394#post193394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's your reasoning for putting Lunars ahead of Abyssals in combat? I disagree mostly because of Lunars' higher charm costs and higher Charm prereqs for basically everything comparable to Solaroids.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems relevant to note that Abyssals... actually don't have a post-soak enhancer before E6 in Melee, which is where Solar power really balloons in the first place (and many of the Ink Monkeys Solar Melee expansions don't actually Mirror back to Abyssals). Their Mirror to Fire-and-Stones Strike is a mediocre Crippling attack. Heavily invested physical combat Lunars, on the other hand, are <i>ridiculously</i> potent (to say nothing of the potency of Withdrawal of Assumptions against CoDs).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T16:57:13-07:00","id":194104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=193987#post193987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spectral and -2 penalty in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure Spectral is gone from their perfect defences now, before that their ass was grass against a Dragon-Blooded who knew what they were doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T20:27:52-07:00","id":194293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=194104#post194104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure Spectral is gone from their perfect defences now, before that their ass was grass against a Dragon-Blooded who knew what they were doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly, Spectral is now completely gone. They are pretty much equal to Solars in combat save for the fact that Solars have a few really good tricks that don't get mirrored, and these probably exceed the Abyssal-unique things. That said, Abyssals can get crazy mote economy going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","name":"Scatters-the-Ashes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T04:59:05-07:00","id":194549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scatters-the-Ashes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=194293#post194293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall correctly, Spectral is now completely gone. They are pretty much equal to Solars in combat save for the fact that Solars have a few really good tricks that don't get mirrored, and these probably exceed the Abyssal-unique things. That said, Abyssals can get crazy mote economy going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their &quot;regain motes for killing people&quot; Charm was changed into giving &quot;attunement motes&quot;, which are not that useful, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T05:34:41-07:00","id":194579,"title":"","content":"I've developed a policy of outright ignoring any passage in 2.5 that uses that phrase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T09:39:48-07:00","id":194700,"title":"","content":"I wonder what evocations might mean for dragonblooded warfare in 3e considering what has been said about what it does to the DBs and armies if they have sword-nukes like that volcanowhatever sword. It might be solar-only to access those effects but then again... *shrug*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T09:51:30-07:00","id":194725,"title":"","content":"Think it was stated that Evocations are not Solar-only, just that Solars are the best at Evocations (and not Solaroids, either, just plain Solars).<br /> <br /> That said, the Evocation tree for Volcano Cutter (from the kickstarter) listed Emerald, Sapphire, and Adamant &quot;tier&quot; evocations on it, and maybe some of those are limited to particular types of splat (like sorcery- DBs only get Emerald, Celestials get Emerald+Sapphire, Solars get all 3) which would be a big reason Solars' Evocation cuisine reigns supreme: if they can unlock all 3 levels on each Artifact.<br /> <br /> But then we also heard that (at least at the time) that DBs are better at Evocations than Sidereals, so who knows at this point. I still wouldn't worry about like an &quot;As In The Beginning&quot; Evocation though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T09:59:34-07:00","id":194737,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are noted as being the worst at Evocations, so Dragon-Blooded may have access to Saphire tier Evocations, if tier is a limitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T10:04:39-07:00","id":194739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=194737#post194737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals are noted as being the worst at Evocations, so Dragon-Blooded may have access to Saphire tier Evocations, if tier is a limitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, hard to say if that will be given the 3e team's explicit repudiation of the hardline tier concepts prevalent in 2e. I mean we don't even know if Evocations are always-on effects or activated with motes like Charms, so the differences may very well come down to mote costing between splats or splats being limited to how many of each type they can unlock on a given weapon, not necessarily &quot;X Exalt gets Emerald only,&quot; etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T11:06:48-07:00","id":194797,"title":"","content":"Since it's artifacts we're talking about it might matter which material which exalt type is using. For example, a fire DB might coax a conflagration evocation almost on the as in the beginning scale out of the red jade family heirloom he/she has spent a DB lifetime using.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T11:21:56-07:00","id":194806,"title":"","content":"It's been said that Dragonblooded have &quot;a special dispensation&quot; where Evocations are concerned. Hereditary equipment may indeed be a component, there.<br /> It's also been hinted that Sidereals -- &quot;worst at Evocations&quot; -- sometimes drop everything to chase falling stars; Starmetal is just that valuable to them.<br /> It's also also been shown that a Solar Charm serves as a prerequisite for a tree branch of the Evocation array previewed in the Kickstarter.<br /> It's also also also been detailed that Lunars' Evocations can't be used when they're in Deadly Beastman Transformation.<br /> <br /> There are probably a lot of factors that go into how and when a given splat can make use of Evocations, aside strict &quot;Emerald, Sapphire, Adamant&quot; breakdowns by splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T11:44:48-07:00","id":194826,"title":"","content":"I would love it if DB evocations could be area effect defenses, protecting the armies they are supposed to lead in order for them to come in to their own. Such effects would tie well into what 2e said about their first age role and the age of sorrows military doctrine. &quot;Hold fast men! That wyld cloud can harm us as long as the roseblack and Her Dark Thorn still protects us! Let the goblins get what's coming to all enemies of Creation and the Scarlet Empress! Charge!!!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T12:32:06-07:00","id":194901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drecain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=194826#post194826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love it if DB evocations could be area effect defenses, protecting the armies they are supposed to lead in order for them to come in to their own. Such effects would tie well into what 2e said about their first age role and the age of sorrows military doctrine. &amp;quot;Hold fast men! That wyld cloud can harm us as long as the roseblack and Her Dark Thorn still protects us! Let the goblins get what's coming to all enemies of Creation and the Scarlet Empress! Charge!!!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> You've got to be careful with that though. In the past DB area attacks have been known to get out of hand really really fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T12:40:59-07:00","id":194912,"title":"","content":"Not area attacks, that's the point. Area defenses that can protect an army..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T14:00:23-07:00","id":194965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=194549#post194549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their &quot;regain motes for killing people&quot; Charm was changed into giving &quot;attunement motes&quot;, which are not that useful, to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They still have the ways available to Solars, ie Ghost-Eating, Bread of Weak Spirit, green jade, etc. It's a wide area attack, so it's easy to replenish it with the motes of the innocent bystanders caught in the crossfire, if you play by RAW. As for me, I've long ago forbidden any mote/wp regeneration, even stunts, from mook-level opposition. It's just too easy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T14:05:21-07:00","id":194969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scatters-the-Ashes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=194293#post194293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall correctly, Spectral is now completely gone. They are pretty much equal to Solars in combat save for the fact that Solars have a few really good tricks that don't get mirrored, and these probably exceed the Abyssal-unique things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssals have some neat tricks on their own. On the other hand, Lunars have keywordless badtouches. Most of the time in 2.5 the fight will depend on respective combat focus/optimization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T00:20:07-07:00","id":195314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=194725#post194725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think it was stated that Evocations are not Solar-only, just that Solars are the best at Evocations (and not Solaroids, either, just plain Solars).<br /> <br /> That said, the Evocation tree for Volcano Cutter (from the kickstarter) listed Emerald, Sapphire, and Adamant &quot;tier&quot; evocations on it, and maybe some of those are limited to particular types of splat (like sorcery- DBs only get Emerald, Celestials get Emerald+Sapphire, Solars get all 3) which would be a big reason Solars' Evocation cuisine reigns supreme: if they can unlock all 3 levels on each Artifact.<br /> <br /> But then we also heard that (at least at the time) that DBs are better at Evocations than Sidereals, so who knows at this point. I still wouldn't worry about like an &quot;As In The Beginning&quot; Evocation though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the thing with the tree there was that some of the charms required a Solar charm as a prereq, which of course only Solars can get. DBs might still get access to higher levels. I'd guess they don't get the top level though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T00:39:56-07:00","id":195317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=195314#post195314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the thing with the tree there was that some of the charms required a Solar charm as a prereq, which of course only Solars can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even there, the Solar Charm prereq might not necessarily mean its associated part of the array is Solars-only. I could see other splats using something analogous in its place, if their themes lend themselves to such a Charm. In that case, the only statement would be that Solars <i>definitely</i> get it, while other splats <i>might</i>, which definitely works fine for &quot;Solars are the masters of Evocations.&quot; Time will tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T11:38:20-07:00","id":195628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=195314#post195314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the thing with the tree there was that some of the charms required a Solar charm as a prereq, which of course only Solars can get. DBs might still get access to higher levels. I'd guess they don't get the top level though.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also said it was meant to be an example, I think, and that Volcano Cutter could have other Evocations? It stands to reason that if Evocations can have native charms as prereqs then we wouldn't see any requiring non-Solar charms in the core, but I wouldn't be surprised to see some that require DB charms in the DB book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T14:48:24-07:00","id":195773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/168314-power-of-dragon-blooded?p=195628#post195628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They also said it was meant to be an example, I think, and that Volcano Cutter could have other Evocations? It stands to reason that if Evocations can have native charms as prereqs then we wouldn't see any requiring non-Solar charms in the core, but I wouldn't be surprised to see some that require DB charms in the DB book.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure about that, if only solars can access adamant circle evocations it wouldn't really make a difference if Tepet Arada's heirloom blade has solar prerequisite charms for its final circle. I actually really like the idea of native charms being the basis for evocations, like your weapon and you are one kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}